top-sort [o_totalprice desc, o_orderdate asc] limit 100
└─ project (c_name, c_custkey, o_orderkey, o_orderdate, o_totalprice, col5) (rows≈1 cost≈13.6K)
   └─ aggregate keys=[customer.c_name, customer.c_custkey, orders.o_orderkey, orders.o_orderdate, orders.o_totalprice] aggs=[sum_0=sum] (rows≈1 cost≈13.6K)
      └─ join inner [lineitem.l_orderkey = orders.o_orderkey] emit-filter 1 from right (rows≈3 cost≈13.4K)
         ├─ source lineitem AS lineitem use-filter 1 keys=[lineitem.l_orderkey] (rows≈10 cost≈120)
         └─ join inner [orders.o_custkey = customer.c_custkey] emit-filter 2 from left (rows≈1 cost≈9K)
            ├─ join left_semi [orders.o_orderkey = __qdb_in__l_orderkey] emit-filter 3 from right (rows≈1 cost≈4.6K)
            │  ├─ source orders AS orders use-filter 3 keys=[orders.o_orderkey] (rows≈10 cost≈200)
            │  └─ project (__qdb_in__l_orderkey) (rows≈1 cost≈280)
            │     └─ filter (> sum_0 315) (rows≈1 cost≈276)
            │        └─ aggregate keys=[lineitem_1.l_orderkey] aggs=[sum_0=sum] (rows≈3 cost≈240)
            │           └─ source lineitem AS lineitem_1 (rows≈10 cost≈120)
            └─ source customer AS customer use-filter 2 keys=[customer.c_custkey] (rows≈10 cost≈200)
